From c9a70f8845ef746f80940b2448fa8228ce8859ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Shaw <robertgshaw2@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:31:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(flowcontrol): add max-saturation-detector composite
 plugin

Add a composite saturation detector that combines the signals of other
saturation detector plugins, reporting pool saturation as the maximum
across its children. This lets flow control gate dispatch on multiple
independent load signals at once - e.g. in-flight concurrency
(concurrency-detector) and scraped queue depth / KV utilization
(utilization-detector) - instead of choosing a single detector.

The plugin resolves its children by name from the plugin handle, so
child detectors must be declared before the composite in the plugins
list. It deliberately implements neither the scheduling Filter
extension point (per-endpoint filtering stays with the children, listed
in profiles explicitly) nor ConsumerPlugin (children are configured
plugins whose data dependencies the framework validates directly).

Each child's signal is also exported through a new
flow_control_detector_saturation gauge, labeled by detector reference
name, so operators can tell which signal is driving
flow_control_pool_saturation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HQoBZWySXyubPdE3crXjzs
